PiG
===

PiG is a Go implementation designed to provide behavior corresponding to the Pi coding-agent project:

https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/

Pi is distributed under the MIT License and carries this notice:

Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner

PiG is not an official release of the upstream Pi project. The upstream maintainers do not endorse PiG. PiG preserves upstream copyright and license notices where applicable. See `LICENSE`, `docs/project/PROVENANCE.md`, the repository SPDX metadata, and this notice.

Embedded third-party software
-----------------------------

PiG embeds the following third-party browser assets in exported HTML transcripts:

- Highlight.js 11.9.0, Copyright (c) 2006, Ivan Sagalaev, BSD-3-Clause.
- Marked 15.0.4, Copyright (c) 2018+, MarkedJS and Copyright (c) 2011-2018, Christopher Jeffrey, MIT; bundled Markdown material is Copyright 2004 John Gruber, BSD-3-Clause.

The Node extension runtime embeds `yaml` 2.9.0, Copyright Eemeli Aro, ISC.

See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` for the applicable license texts. Dependencies included in a release are recorded in that release's SPDX SBOM.

PiG also contains a Go port of `grok-mermaid` 0.2.2 and data generated from its width table:

- Source: <https://github.com/xl0/grok-mermaid/tree/v0.2.2>
- Copyright 2023-2026 SpaceXAI
- Copyright 2026 Alexey Zaytsev
- License: Apache-2.0

The generated width table also derives from `unicode-width` 0.2.0, Copyright (c) 2015 The Rust Project Developers, used under its MIT option.

PiG ports upstream Pi code that incorporates material from OpenTUI, `ansi-regex`, and `strip-ansi`. Their notices are retained in the corresponding source files and in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

The project banner and derived social banners adapt the Go gopher, which was designed by Renee French and is licensed under CC-BY-4.0. The license text is in `LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt`.

`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` adapts Contributor Covenant 2.1 under CC-BY-4.0. Its source and attribution are retained in that document and in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

